WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.370
I want to talk today about something that
will become a bigger and bigger issue over

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:09.280
the next couple of years when it comes to
the things that Joe Biden and Democrats want

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.650
to do and the fact that there will be resistance
from the Republican Party, that's not like

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:21.410
the typical resistance we've seen in the past
from more traditional Republicans, but a more

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:27.050
sort of pernicious and extreme resistance,
which completely poisons the well for people

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.860
that want to have good faith debates about
what policy should be.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.590
And I think the best way to sort of explain
what I'm talking about is to imagine it through

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.130
the lens of one issue.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.580
Let's pick pick the issue of taxes to discuss
this just for the sake of selecting something.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:48.750
There is no one right answer on what tax rates
should be and what tax brackets should be

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:54.010
and what should be tax deductions versus tax
credits versus nothing at all.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.170
These are real topics over which there is
serious debate.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.370
There's a lot of academic literature, for
example, which suggests the top marginal tax

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:08.030
rate for generating the most government revenue
should be 70 percent.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:12.480
But beyond that, it can start to be a disincentive
for people to work.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:19.340
But even if you agree on 70 percent, what
level of income should that rate kick in?

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.780
Should it be two million dollars a year or
10 or 20 million dollars a year?

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:28.510
There are really good debates there that that's
not there's not one answer to that question.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:34.900
There are real debates as to whether lower
no income tax states are really cheaper to

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:38.070
live in or in a state with no income tax.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.890
Are you saving on income tax?

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:43.990
But there's higher sales tax on average and
higher property tax on average.

00:01:43.990 --> 00:01:50.409
So, like, is a no income tax state really
cheaper overall or is it just an illusion

00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:53.140
meant to attract people with a political statement?

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:56.330
We have no state income tax when you pay more
in other types of taxes.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.830
OK, that's a great thing to explore.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.140
We can debate whether people should pay any
taxes at all if they earn under ten thousand

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.440
dollars a year or twenty thousand dollars
a year or thirty thousand dollars a year,

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:14.950
or should they get a tax credit versus a low
tax rate, or where should phaseouts begin

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:19.500
for certain programs, welfare programs or
tax credits or whatever?

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:21.250
What about universal basic income?

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:26.069
There are good debates being had there and
all of these are debates that can be had in

00:02:26.069 --> 00:02:29.209
good faith with people who disagree about
the answer.

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:32.610
Like I have an opinion about all of those
issues and I recognize there are people with

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.440
other opinions who are discussing these issues
in good faith.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.910
They're operating within the realm of what's
reasonable.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.190
They have valid points to make and these are
the people we need to engage with.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:49.860
The problem here is when extremists poison
the well by introducing ideas that, aside

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.300
from making no sense, are never going to be
a reality.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:03:01.319
So like when you interject the people who
say all taxes are theft or all taxes are slavery

00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:06.690
as a starting point or all taxes should be
abolished as a starting point, this is the

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:07.860
United States.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:11.160
This is a country of three hundred and thirty
one million people.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.000
We're not getting rid of all taxes.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.520
The idea of taxes is slavery is not going
to push the debate forward as to what tax

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.910
policy should be or people who say, you know,
we should put a 99 percent tax on incomes

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:24.300
over a million dollars.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:27.290
No one should be allowed to make over a million
dollars.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.030
It's not going to happen, guys.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.440
We're getting nowhere with that is the starting
point.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:39.480
And I'm going to distinguish in a moment extremis
poisoning the well versus productive stretching

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.900
of the Overton Window.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.670
These are two different things.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:50.910
So the people who say, you know, these things,
they are often asserting that we should include

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:57.110
these ideas because we don't want to suppress
speech and we don't want to censor ideas.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.160
I agree with that.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:03.849
But as I've said before, not every harebrained
idea deserves a seat at the adult table when

00:04:03.849 --> 00:04:05.769
we're discussing policy.

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:09.170
So we often talk about moving the Overton
Window, for example.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:13.840
The more we talk about Medicare for all is
the gold standard, the more a public option

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.979
seems to be a centrist idea, which it is.

00:04:16.979 --> 00:04:22.669
The more we talk about two thousand dollars
per month in coronavirus stimulus, the more

00:04:22.669 --> 00:04:27.160
that a single two thousand dollar payment
seems like a pretty centrist idea, which it

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.160
is.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:32.900
And so we want to use the Overton Window to
better our negotiating ability.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.979
But taxes are slavery doesn't improve anyone's
negotiating ability.

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:39.279
It's just a crazy idea.

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:44.270
And this is how these new extremists in the
House of Representatives are going to be poisoning

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:50.520
the well, not necessarily on taxes, but this
is the idea of it and making it impossible

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.800
for Democrats to do anything which they've
admitted they plan to do.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:59.330
So as a result, as we spoke about yesterday,
I'm completely on.

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:04.550
Board with what we learned Bernie Sanders
plans to do, and that's used budget reconciliation

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.720
to get as much done as possible in the Senate
with a simple majority rather than requiring

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:12.680
60 votes, meaning they don't need a single
Republican.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:18.610
Assuming that all 50 Democrats are on the
same page, there unfortunately is no other

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.370
way with people who are fundamentally bad
faith actors.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:27.129
Now, I'm willing to have my mind changed,
but what good will the idea of bipartisanship

00:05:27.129 --> 00:05:33.069
do when it just means allowing completely
ridiculous ideas to be part of the conversation

00:05:33.069 --> 00:05:38.090
and completely absurd people to slow down
the possibility of progress?

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:42.340
So there's the debate about the filibuster
that continues.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:47.300
There's the idea of unity and bipartisanship
that Joe Biden has expressed as a goal.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.400
As I've said before, I don't think it's going
to happen.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.680
And this is exactly why these extremist ideas
poison the well.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.409
And we're seeing it happen already on Fox
News.

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:00.460
We're seeing it on OMON, we're seeing it on
Newsmax.

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:06.779
And I believe that while I am willing to have
my mind changed, the idea of bipartisanship,

00:06:06.779 --> 00:06:12.779
merely if that means allowing ridiculous radical
reactionary ideas into the debate does nothing

00:06:12.779 --> 00:06:14.259
good for anybody.

00:06:14.259 --> 00:06:19.270
And Democrats should simply plow through it
for these next at least two years during which

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:21.849
they will have control of the House, Senate
and the White House.

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:23.909
If you disagree with me, let me know

